# Build directories
build/
build-*/
buildWindows/
examples/build/
tests/build/

# CMake generated files
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile
*.cmake
!cmake/*.cmake
!cmake/toolchains/
!cmake/toolchains/*.cmake
!cmake/patches/
!cmake/patches/*.cmake

# ...and the CMake-level tests, which are scripts CTest runs rather than build output. Without this
# `git add` skips them silently and the tests fail on CI with "Not a file", which is how this line
# came to exist.
!tests/cmake/*.cmake

# Compiled binaries
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.lib

# Compiled shaders
*.spv

# Evidence pipeline: baked, byte-verified artifacts under generated/ are
# committed on purpose (package.json / report.json / sidecar payloads,
# which may include *.spv, *.cmake, or other otherwise-ignored extensions).
!generated/**

# ...and so are the source assets a recipe names. A shader recipe points at SPIR-V compiled once
# by hand and checked in, rather than compiled during the build: glslangValidator's output varies
# between its own versions, so building it would make every committed package depend on whichever
# shader compiler the CI image shipped. The *.spv rule above would otherwise swallow them.
!recipes/**

# CI-downloaded SDKs that land inside the checkout instead of a temp dir.
# humbletim/setup-vulkan-sdk extracts to $GITHUB_WORKSPACE/VULKAN_SDK on Windows
# (confirmed from a real CI run: VULKAN_SDK=D:/a/MduX/MduX/VULKAN_SDK, i.e. the
# repo root) rather than $RUNNER_TEMP, which the "Verify no source-tree writes"
# check below correctly flagged as an untracked write. Ignoring it here is the
# fix, not changing the action - there's no documented input to redirect its
# extraction path.
/VULKAN_SDK/

# IDE and editor files
.vs/
.vscode/
*.suo
*.user
*.sln.docstates

# Local reference material - never committed.
#
# The whole directory, not selected paths inside it. Five specific sub-paths were listed here
# until issue #116, which left inputs/CMake/ and any newly-added folder under
# inputs/Documentation/ untracked-but-not-ignored - so a `git add -A` would have committed them.
# That is the exact class of content #7 and #23 spent a history rewrite removing, and ADR-006
# forbids outright. A directory-level rule cannot be defeated by adding a file to it.
#
# This lives in the *first* PR of the #116 stack rather than the last, because the narrow rule
# actually caught someone out while that stack was in review: a `git add -A` on this branch staged
# `inputs/CMake` as a gitlink. It was a one-line SHA rather than the 431 MB behind it, and it was
# amended out before anyone pulled, but a guard that lands after the thing it guards against is
# not a guard.
inputs/

# Temporary files
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
*~

# Vendor-specific AI coding agent instructions (local only).
# AGENTS.md is the canonical, vendor-neutral instruction source - keep it tracked.
CLAUDE.md
.clauderules
.cursorrules
.cursor/
.windsurfrules
.windsurf/
.aider.conf.yml
.aiderrules
.aider.chat.history.md
.clinerules
.clinerules/
.continuerules
.continue/
.codeium/
.amazonq/
.junie/
.roorules
.roo/
GEMINI.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Python bytecode from the host-only lint tools (tools/docs-lint, tools/evidence-lint).
# CI sets PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, but a local run of the self-tests still leaves these behind.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Ephemeral exact-SHA checkout of the shared MedUI conformance contract in CI.
.medui-conformance/
